{"name":"Italian Buckthorn","hex":"#6b8c23","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"buckthorn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several, often thorny shrubs or small trees, especially\nthe buckthorn family (Rhamnaceae),\nespecially genus Rhamnus,\nespecially common buckthorn or purging buckthorn (Rhamnus cathartica).\nalso alder buckthorn (Frangula), especially Frangula alnus).\nsea buckthorn (Hippophae, in family Elaeagnaceae).","the buckthorn family (Rhamnaceae),\nespecially genus Rhamnus,\nespecially common buckthorn or purging buckthorn (Rhamnus cathartica).\nalso alder buckthorn (Frangula), especially Frangula alnus)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buckthorn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rhamnus alaternus","blocks":[{"text":"Rhamnus alaternus is a species of flowering plant in the buckthorn family Rhamnaceae, known by the common names Italian buckthorn or Mediterranean buckthorn. It is a hardy medium-sized evergreen shrub with fragrant flowers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Rhamnus_alaternus_%288692911406%29.jpg/330px-Rhamnus_alaternus_%288692911406%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhamnus_alaternus","wikidata":"Q721200"},{"title":"Rhamnus (plant)","blocks":[{"text":"Rhamnus is a genus of about 140 accepted species of shrubs or small trees, commonly known as buckthorns, in the family Rhamnaceae. Its species range from 1 to 10 m tall and are native mainly in East Asia and North America, but found throughout the temperate and subtropical Northern Hemisphere, and also more locally in the subtropical Southern Hemisphere in parts of Africa and South America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Rhamnus_cathartica_f%C3%BCr_Wikipedia.jpg/330px-Rhamnus_cathartica_f%C3%BCr_Wikipedia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en